Inclusions focus on primary diagnostic accuracy evaluations of rapid point-of-care Chlamydia trachomatis tests in 
nonpregnant reproductive-age populations, using NAAT as reference. Where the abstract suggests NAAT was among the 
comparators but the reference standard or 2x2 reporting was unclear (e.g., composite standards or prototype 
evaluations), studies were INCLUDED conservatively for resolution at full-text. Clear non-DTA, epidemiologic, review, or
guideline articles were EXCLUDED. Key borderline cases: study 28 (composite reference despite PCR on all) and study 49 
(prototype; feasibility with evolving sensitivity), both included with low confidence for later verification.
